From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] kernelbase: pass the WCHAR count to GetEnvironmentVariableW
 in hack_shrink_environment

Valve's WINE_SHRINK_ENV hack (patches/wine-valve 0059) reads
WINE_SHRINK_ENV and SteamGameId into a WCHAR str[40] but passes
sizeof(str), 80, as its size in characters. A value of 41 to 79
characters, which the player can set for either variable on a game's
page, is copied whole and overruns the buffer on the stack, in every
process of a Steam game on its first GetEnvironmentStringsW call. Pass
ARRAY_SIZE(str): a longer value then leaves str empty.
Proton ships the same code.

Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-09-28-steam-game-id.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 dlls/kernelbase/process.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/kernelbase/process.c b/dlls/kernelbase/process.c
index 31a1c2c..02495eb 100644
--- a/dlls/kernelbase/process.c
+++ b/dlls/kernelbase/process.c
@@ -1674,9 +1674,9 @@ static void hack_shrink_environment( WCHAR *env, SIZE_T len )
         WCHAR str[40];
 
         *str = 0;
-        if (GetEnvironmentVariableW( L"WINE_SHRINK_ENV", str, sizeof(str)) )
+        if (GetEnvironmentVariableW( L"WINE_SHRINK_ENV", str, ARRAY_SIZE(str)) )
             enabled = *str != '0';
-        else if (GetEnvironmentVariableW( L"SteamGameId", str, sizeof(str)) )
+        else if (GetEnvironmentVariableW( L"SteamGameId", str, ARRAY_SIZE(str)) )
             enabled = !wcscmp( str, L"431590" );
         else
             enabled = 0;
-- 
2.55.0

